"IH",23,56,"explicit"],["lambda","x",13,57,"explicit"],["apply",21,58],["constant","List.nil",[["param","u_1"]]],["apply",60,13],["apply",59,61],["apply",62,1],["lambda","l",12,63,"explicit"],["lambda","inst._@.Batteries.Data.List.Basic.2569134358._hygCtx._hyg.9",9,64,"instance"],["lambda","R",5,65,"explicit"],["lambda","α",0,66,"implicit"]],"project":false,"range":{"column":0,"endColumn":66,"endLine":585,"line":576},"type":18,"typeText":"{α : Type u_1} → (R : α → α → Prop) → [DecidableRel.{u_1 + 1, u_1 + 1} R] → List.{u_1} α → List.{u_1} α","unsafe":false,"value":67,"source":{"code":"/--\n`pwFilter R l` is a maximal sublist of `l` which is `Pairwise R`.\n`pwFilter (·≠·)` is the erase duplicates function (cf. `eraseDup`), and `pwFilter (·<·)` finds\na maximal increasing subsequence in `l`. For example,\n```\npwFilter (·<·) [0, 1, 5, 2, 6, 3, 4] = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]\n```\n-/\ndef pwFilter (R : α → α → Prop) [DecidableRel R] (l : List α) : List α :=\n  l.foldr (fun x IH => if ∀ y ∈ IH, R x y then x :: IH else IH) []","start":576,"end":585},"axioms":[]}